Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 12:28:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/23] testsuite: Add Bugzilla reporter attribution to
 pr79524.f90 [PR fortran/79524]

Retrospective attribution header added as part of a manual
Bugzilla-provenance audit on 2026-04-22 (meta-repo tracking commit
40f0a94; GitHub issues on krystophny/gcc-dev).  The existing GCC
Fortran testsuite convention (see pr113363.f90, pdt_50.f03,
arrayio_4.f90) uses an in-file "! Contributed by ..." line; practice
is inconsistent and attribution is not strictly required for small
Bugzilla reducers, but we are adding it retroactively for provenance
safety and completeness.  No behavioural change.

Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
Assisted-by: GPT (OpenAI)

	PR fortran/79524

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gfortran.dg/pr79524.f90: Add reporter attribution header.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
---
 gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr79524.f90 | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr79524.f90 b/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr79524.f90
index 0b2bfe092ad..abd5c263bcc 100644
--- a/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr79524.f90
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr79524.f90
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 ! { dg-do compile }
 ! { dg-set-target-env-var MALLOC_PERTURB_ "165" }
 ! PR fortran/79524
+! Contributed by David Binderman  <dcb314@hotmail.com>
 ! Reject parameter arrays with variable-length CHARACTER elements without
 ! leaving the temporary charlen from the failed declaration on cl_list.
 program p
